# Dagric OS Pro — Gaming & Windows-app compatibility
# Run Windows software and games without leaving Dagric.

# Wine: the Windows compatibility layer (32-bit support for classic
# .exe installers is added by the pro-edition hook via i386 multiarch)
wine
winetricks

# THE PIECE THAT MAKES A .exe DOUBLE-CLICKABLE, AND IT WAS NEVER INSTALLED.
#
# wine-binfmt registers the PE format with the kernel (/usr/lib/binfmt.d/wine
# plus /usr/share/binfmts/wine) so a Windows executable can simply be RUN.
# Without it Wine is present and a .exe is an inert file: Dolphin offers
# "Open with...", nothing happens on a double-click, and the switcher's entire
# mental model of installing software — download setup, double-click it —
# fails at the first step.
#
# It is only a SUGGESTS of wine, so --apt-recommends false was never going to
# bring it in, and nothing pinned it. Confirmed in out/build-pro.log: the name
# appears exactly once, inside apt's "Suggested packages:" block, and "Setting
# up wine-binfmt" appears nowhere.
#
# This is a promise gap in the PAID tier, which is the worst place to have one.
# The shipped guide tells Pro owners in as many words that Wine "runs many .exe
# files on a double-click", and docs/EDITIONS.md sells "run classic .exe
# software". Neither could be true.
wine-binfmt

# NOTE: Steam is deliberately NOT preinstalled (Valve's EULA — owner
# mandate: proprietary stores are never bundled). It installs only via the
# dagric-get-steam consent helper in the Hub; the 0600 hook pre-enables
# i386 multiarch + 32-bit Wine/Vulkan so that consent install works
# instantly when the owner opts in.

# Vulkan drivers — CRITICAL: Proton/DXVK translate DirectX to Vulkan; with
# --apt-recommends false nothing else pulls these in, and without them Steam
# games fall back to slow OpenGL or fail. 32-bit Vulkan for older games is
# added by the 0600 hook alongside wine32. (Found by friendly-Debian review.)
mesa-vulkan-drivers
vulkan-tools

# Performance: CPU/GPU governor optimization while gaming + FPS overlay
gamemode
mangohud
# GUI to configure the MangoHud overlay without editing config files
goverlay

# Lutris — the standard launcher for non-Steam games and Windows game
# installers (Battle.net, EA, Ubisoft). Makes "gaming edition" credible
# beyond Steam. (Epic/GOG via Heroic is a future consent-helper — not in
# Debian.) Found by test review: Steam-only felt half-finished for the tier.
lutris

# THE HALVES --apt-recommends false DROPPED, AND WHY EACH ONE MATTERS.
#
# lutris Recommends python3-evdev and fluidsynth and neither arrived. evdev is
# how Lutris enumerates controllers at all, so the joypad list in its settings
# was empty on a machine sold on gaming. fluidsynth is MIDI playback, which a
# surprising number of the 1990s Windows titles Wine exists to run depend on for
# their soundtrack.
python3-evdev
fluidsynth

# DXVK translates Direct3D 9/10/11 to Vulkan. dagric-gaming teaches
# "wine setup.exe" as the headline Pro capability and docs/EDITIONS.md sells
# running classic .exe software; a bare Wine prefix on Debian uses WineD3D,
# which renders D3D through OpenGL and is routinely several times slower and
# buggier. Debian packages DXVK in trixie main, so unlike Proton it is
# redistributable and can be bundled outright.
#
# BOTH HALVES ARE NAMED ON PURPOSE. dxvk Depends is
# "dxvk-wine64 | dxvk-wine32" and Recommends is "dxvk-wine32, dxvk-wine64", so
# with Recommends off, listing dxvk alone silently satisfies the alternative
# with the 64-bit half only. The classic .exe games this is for are 32-bit, so
# that would install the feature and miss the case. dxvk-wine32 is architecture
# i386 and therefore CANNOT come through this file at all; it is on the 0600
# hook's multiarch line, after dpkg --add-architecture i386.
dxvk
dxvk-wine64
